WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:50.360
[Music]

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:59.660
[Narrator:] Allow us to present Mr. and Mrs. Josiah Smith, average Americans of a half-century ago.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.780
Younger than the average Americans of today,

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:08.960
but then their chances of growing to a ripe old age were clouded with many threats.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:17.400
[Dramatic music]

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.000
The last 50 years, the sky has been cleared

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.840
of many of yesterday's perils, and today, the average American lives longer,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.620
but it's well-recognized that medical science,

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:33.380
while helping him live longer, [?] pretty fair on the whole.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.520
But, while there's very little smallpox now, there's 
plenty of high blood pressure.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.840
[Beating drums representing the heart]

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:51.120
Diphtheria is rare now, but the spreading waistline 
is spreading [stretching sound], and along with it,

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.800
troubles of the heart, kidneys, and blood vessels,

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:58.240
and other problems of a constantly-aging 
population.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.420
For the control of many of these conditions, early 
detection is important.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:07.920
Therefore, recent years have seen increasing 
interest in mass-screening devices.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.040
For example, diabetes detection drives using blood sugar tests

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.120
or urine sugar tests have been tried in 
many communities.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:22.900
The idea is to screen apparently-well people not already under their doctor's care.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.400
Objective tests are used.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.580
Those with sugar findings above a specific standard are referred to their physicians.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:37.180
Thus, many unsuspected cases have received 
early attention from their doctors.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.880
But to avoid the duplication of effort in screening

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:47.840
one month for diabetes, another month for tuberculosis,

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:56.540
and another for syphilis, the question has been asked, why not combine various screening tests?

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:02.940
Instead of many separate screening lines, why not 
combine them into one multiple screening?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:09.520
Multiple screening makes use of a series of technical tests, each taking less than three minutes.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.200
Multiple screening does not involve diagnosis.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.260
The idea is to sift from apparently-well people,

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.780
those who may have a latent disease or an unrecognized disability,

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.500
and to refer them to their physicians.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.700
Wherever such a project is carried out,

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.560
the local medical society will help select the tests that are included.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.960
A multiple-screening project can be done on a small or a large scale to suit community needs.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.080
For example, if blood is to be taken for a syphilis case-finding project,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:46.020
such blood samples can also be examined for diabetes and anemia.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.520
This is multiple screening in one of its simplest 
forms.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.680
If it is decided to add x-ray, the x-rays can be read for tuberculosis,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.900
for certain heart abnormalities, and even for lung cancer.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.980
If it is decided to use urine sugar tests for 
diabetes, rather than blood sugar tests,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.160
the urine can also be examined for nephritis.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.560
Other tests that can be added are height and weight,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.980
hearing and vision tests,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.060
blood pressure tests,

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.640
oral examinations,

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.840
and perhaps electrocardiographs

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.980
New tests can be added as they are developed.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.660
A community can select almost any combination of tests it wishes.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:39.020
In one rural program, two tests were used. In an 
urban area, four tests were used.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.280
In another urban area, seven tests were used.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.580
This is a matter for local decision.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:49.340
Each community can develop a multiple-screening 
project to suit its own needs.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.840
The personnel needed for multiple screening includes

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:58.400
some administrative personnel, laboratory personnel,

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.640
and the personnel at the testing center or centers.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:05.300
An average testing center needs a receptionist,

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:10.720
several technicians, several clerks, and a supervisor.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.020
These can be arranged in any convenient order.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:20.140
Such a testing center can screen in one day 
several hundred Mr. and Mrs. Joe Smiths.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.860
Mr. Smith arrives. The tests begin.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:33.220
Each test must be inexpensive to use, as specific 
as possible, and quickly done.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.580
Joe Smith spends only about three minutes on 
each test in the screening line.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.220
Technicians do the testing.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:46.780
At the end of the line, he is reminded that any positive reports will be sent to his own physician.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.660
This saves the most highly-trained type of personnel,

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:56.220
the physician, for the later work of interpretation, diagnosis, and treatment.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.020
Thus, through multiple screening, economical and

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:04.480
effective mass case-finding may be provided in any community.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:11.200
From the general population, the tests screen out those who appear to need medical supervision.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.740
These are referred to their own physicians.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:19.080
A few of them, of course, may be found by their physicians to be well.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.600
The others will be diagnosed as ill, and treatment begun.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.980
Multiple screening can channel to physicians

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:32.480
people with unsuspected serious diseases or minor disabilities

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:36.840
early enough to stabilize, if not actually to correct the condition.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:42.220
Many late complications can be avoided through early diagnosis and treatment.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.500
The private physician of today, because of the rising

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.520
importance of the chronic diseases, is in a dilemma.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:55.360
Watching the stream of humanity passing his door, he knows that in his community,

00:06:55.360 --> 00:07:04.940
there are unknown cases of tuberculosis, of diabetes, of syphilis, of glaucoma, of heart disease.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.720
He knows that many of them will not of their own accord

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:12.060
seek medical attention until disease has won a firm foothold.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:18.240
He also knows that if he could find and treat them 
at any early stage, he could help them.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.300
What can the physician do?

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:26.500
Ethics forbid him to put up a sign to warn or persuade them.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.640
He cannot seek them out or call out to them.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:34.540
He must stand aside and remain silent.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:41.900
But multiple screening as a community project can do what must be done to combat the chronic diseases.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:48.340
It can turn some of the people, the ones in need of early attention, back to their own doctor's door.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:56.440
So, the idea of multiple screening is to use mass-screening devices on people in general;

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:02.560
people who feel well, to bring unsuspected cases 
to their own physicians

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:07.300
early enough to prevent complications or crippling illness.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.460
Early enough to protect their health while they have it.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:27.260
[Music]

